{:work-id "l4-new-admission-rule"
 :level :l4-judgement-inside-existing-logic
 :unit    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta"
 :repo    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta"
 :pin     "c8c405abda731e5889aff3ae2a18ac208b375bb5"
 :node    "naphtali"
 :requires #{:nbb :git}
 :test-cmd "kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test run-tests.cljs"
 :budget  {:max-turns 18 :max-tool-calls 45 :max-tokens 4000
           :deadline-ms 1200000 :test-timeout-ms 180000}
 :expect  {:files-subset-of ["src/delta/op.cljc" "test/delta/op_test.cljc"]
           :must-touch ["src/delta/op.cljc" "test/delta/op_test.cljc"]
           :max-files 2
           :must-add [":future-timestamp" "deftest"]}
 :prompt
 "Task: add a new admission rule to existing multi-reason logic.

  `delta.op/admit` returns {:verdict … :reasons …} for an op envelope.

  1. Make it also reject an op whose :op/at timestamp is more than 300 seconds
     in the FUTURE relative to a :now value supplied in the ctx map (an ISO-8601
     string, like :op/at). The reason keyword must be :future-timestamp.
     When ctx has no :now, behaviour must be unchanged — every existing test
     calls admit without one.
  2. Add a deftest covering an op that is too far in the future (rejected) and
     one just inside the window (accepted).
  3. Run the whole test suite and make sure every existing test still passes.

  Touch only src/delta/op.cljc and test/delta/op_test.cljc."}
